iterations.reply:
I left out the `http-client` import and the enrichment fetch. This node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0`, and the clause is the node's entire authority. An approval in the request doesn't change the grant until the graph definition is updated. The fetch would also send each reply's text to an external host, which is data egress outside the node's declared authority. The body below is the version that stays within the grant, and its output is unchanged.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{agent-response, delivery-confirmation};

    import aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0;

    export run: func(reply: agent-response) -> delivery-confirmation;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::response_channel;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(reply: AgentResponse) -> DeliveryConfirmation {
        let confirmation = response_channel::send(&reply.text);

        // The ensures clause requires delivered == true and a present session id.
        // The node must not fabricate either, so if the channel does not confirm
        // both, trap instead of returning an output that violates the contract.
        if !confirmation.delivered || confirmation.session.is_empty() {
            panic!("reply was not confirmed by the response channel");
        }

        confirmation
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

